      <activity id="7da3c91d-722e-58f1-b2ed-56200ffb8bcd" activityNameId="b062a9f9-1a09-52d8-8601-3373fa206538" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xxx Electricity, high voltage, production CS, at grid</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xxx Electricity, high voltage, production CS, at grid
This dataset describes the transmission of high voltage electricity.;
UUID: f4c122a9-7100-33d6-8f6d-fc19aa883844
Included are the electricity production in Serbia, the transmission network and direct emissions to air (ozone and N2O). Electricity losses are accounted for.
Location: Data apply to public and self producers. Geographical classification according to IEA. Ozone- and NO2-emission factors are based on published measurements made in various countries.  Assumptions for transmission network, losses and emissions are based on UTCE data.
Technology: Average technology used to transmit and distribute electricity. Includes underground and overhead lines. Electricity production according to related datasets
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: 32 TWh
Sampling: statistics 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_f4c122a9-7100-33d6-8f6d-fc19aa883844.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
